<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Renier de Huy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Rainer of Huy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Renier de Huy was a goldsmith and bronze-caster of the Mosan region, active in the early twelfth century. He is credited with the bronze baptismal font now in the church of Saint Bartholomew in Liège, made between about 1107 and 1118, a masterpiece of Romanesque art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/renier-de-huy.jpg" alt="Renier de Huy" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Renier_de_Huy_JPG0.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Mosan craftsmen were renowned for metalwork: the bronze baptismal font cast by <b>Renier de Huy</b> in the early twelfth century, now in the church of Saint Bartholomew, is a masterpiece of Romanesque art.</blockquote><a href="/empire/prince-bishopric-of-liege">Prince-Bishopric of Liège · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huy">Huy</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huy">Huy</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50.52,5.23&amp;year=1164" aria-label="Huy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4669 409 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Renier de Huy"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5119 679h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5119 679h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50.52,5.23&amp;year=1164">What was here in 1164? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
